# g96-be-tui-ui: the footer status, idle auto-clear and pending-resume feed of the Node TUI, now in mixdog-core-session.

## 1. Surface (nothing to apply in a hot file; no Cargo edge, no protocol row, no SERVICE_PENDING name)

New public modules of `mixdog_core_session::session` (registered in `session/mod.rs`, which is not a hot file). Each takes what it reads as
parsed values or through a small trait, so nothing here does file I/O: the compose supplies the readers (through the I/O lanes).

- `statusline_claude`: `read_claude_code_current_route(&dyn ClaudeWorld, &ClaudeSources) -> ClaudeRoute`. Sources: the config dir's
  `settings.json`, the data dir's `claude-current-model.json` and the config dir's `cc-statusline-last.json` (each with its mtime;
  `PERSISTED_MAX_AGE_MS` is the ten-minute age limit), the request payload. `ClaudeWorld` = catalog window of a model
  (`CatalogService::sync_meta(id, "anthropic-oauth")["contextWindow"]`), the `anthropic-oauth` roster rows
  (`CatalogService::cached_models("anthropic-oauth")`), and the environment (`ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_<FAMILY>_MODEL`).
- `gateway_routes`: reader side `read_session_route(&store, id, pid, fallback_legacy)`, `read_latest_host_route(&store, pid, exclude)`,
  `normalize_route_section`, over the parsed `gateway-session-routes.json` (the writer keeps its queue; a reader needs no lock).
- `statusline_limits`: `build_gateway_limits(&LimitsInput, &mut RouteSection, route, provider_out, usage_snapshot)` and `UsageView` (the
  incremental view of `gateway-usage.local.jsonl`: `refresh(file_identity, size, read_range)` then `load(now)`). `LimitsInput` takes the
  config's `gateway` and `agent` sections and the loaded events. The route section is the one the usage writer owns:
  `GatewayUsage::with_route_section(|section| ..)` (new), so route spend and the recorded summaries agree on when a route began.
- `statusline_status`: `load_gateway_status(&dyn StatusWorld, &StatusInput) -> Option<Value>`, `compact_boundary_for_status`,
  `cached_quota_windows_fallback`, `format_gateway_limit_segments(&Value, &SegmentFormat) -> Vec<String>`. `StatusWorld` = catalog metadata
  (`CatalogService::sync_meta`), the cached model row of `<data>/<provider>-models.json` (`openai-oauth-models.json`,
  `anthropic-oauth-models.json`, `grok-oauth-models.json`), and `inherited_route()` (the call above). `StatusInput` carries `mixdog-config.json`,
  the config dir's `settings.json`, `gateway-session-routes.json`, `gateway-oauth-usage-cache.json` and this process's start time.
- `statusline_agents`: `agent_statusline_payload`, `classify_agent_workers`, `active_hidden_agent_workers`, `agent_web_search_status` over
  the agent registry's rows (`RuntimeEntry` / `RuntimeSession` are plain rows to fill from `AgentSessions`) and the hidden agent names of
  `internal-agents` (`listHiddenAgentNames`).
- `idle_auto_clear`: `AutoClear<H: AutoClearHost>` (before submit / before wake / perform), `idle_auto_clear_due`,
  `session_activity_timestamp`. The host is the thread: busy, queue length, `compact({requireReduction: true})` (the existing
  `thread/compact/start` path), the cleared-view application, notices.
- `pending_resume`: `PendingResume<H: ResumeHost>` (kick / flush_deferred / discard) and `execution_resume_key`, `short_text_fingerprint`.
- `FilePromptHistory` now holds the per-cwd lists in memory (bounded, 128 cwds, `MIXDOG_PROMPT_HISTORY_CACHE_LIMIT` at least 8); nothing to wire.
- `mixdog_core_config::workflow::with_default_presets` (new, public): `withDefaultPresets`.

## 2. What the compose does with them (a later wiring task; none of it changes a protocol)

- The footer is built by the front end from `load_gateway_status` + `build_gateway_limits` + `format_gateway_limit_segments` once a protocol
  method for it exists; no new method is added here. Until a surface calls them nothing runs, so nothing is off.
- The idle auto-clear is driven from the place a submit and a completion wake enter a thread (`auto_clear_before_submit(false)` before the
  submit, `auto_clear_before_wake()` before the wake turn). `thread/compact/start` stays the compaction.

## 3. SERVICE_PENDING

Nothing to remove.
